INT. JUNE'S BEDROOM - NIGHT

Posters, fairy lights, a pile of laundry that is definitely not just laundry. JUNE PARK, 16, sits on the bed in pajamas with her best friend WESLEY, 17, and her little brother BEN, 9, who is holding a flashlight he was told not to touch.

JUNE
(whispering, tugging a blanket over all three of them)
Okay so the rule is nobody screams. If somebody screams we all die.

WESLEY
(also whispering, much louder)
That is not how that works.

BEN
(clicking the flashlight on and off)
It is exactly how that works.

The phone BUZZES on the nightstand. June jumps. Wesley shrieks and ducks under a pillow.

JUNE
(snatching it, glaring at him)
You screamed!

WESLEY
(muffled)
I did not scream I sneezed in a very high register.

ON PHONE: "MOM: Honey are you asleep? Door's locked right?"

JUNE
(texting back with her thumbs flying)
Mom is checking on me. Act asleep.

BEN
(flopping dramatically onto the pillow)
Zzzz. Zzzz. Why am I the one doing the snoring?

WESLEY
(jabbing a finger at him)
Because you're the most convincing.

A door SLAMS somewhere in the house. All three freeze.

MOM (V.O.)
(through the phone, tinny, on speaker now)
June? Is that you in the hall?

JUNE
(going pale, the phone trembling in her hand)
Mom, I'm in my room.

MOM (V.O.)
(slowly)
Then who just walked past my door?

The closet door CREAKS open. From the shadows, a tall figure in a shower curtain hobbles out, dragging one foot, groaning.

AUNT LIN, 40s, June's aunt, ghoul makeup smeared, grinning.

AUNT LIN
(throwing off the curtain)
Surprise! Happy Halloween eve!

WESLEY
(throwing the pillow, shrieking)
I hate this family!

JUNE
(laughing, hitting her with the blanket)
Aunt Lin! You almost killed us!

BEN
(shining the flashlight in her face)
You look dead. It's great.

AUNT LIN
(accepting a pillow to the face)
I've been rehearsing since Tuesday.

MOM (V.O.)
(sighing)
I told her not to. Goodnight, everyone.
